[profiles.guide]
notes = '''This is the gyro variant: tilting the controller moves the cursor, as a fine pointer next to the right stick {rs}. Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller.
The right stick {rs} moves the cursor: {rt} selects (left click, hold to drag a box), and {lt} moves, attacks or captures a point (right click). The left stick {ls} scrolls the map, and {up} {down} zoom.
{south} is attack move (then click the target with {rt}), {west} stops and {north} reinforces the selected squad. {left} jumps to the next builder, {right} to idle military. Click {l3} for the next unit type in the selection.
Hold {lb} for the control groups and aim the right stick {rs} at one: release to select it. Hold {lb} and {rb} together to put the selection in a group instead (Ctrl + number).
{rb} is Shift: hold it to queue orders or add to the selection. Abilities, stances and wargear are the buttons on the taskbar: click them with {rt}.
Click {r3} for the other unit commands (move, melee, attack ground, build, attach, unload, repair, leader, scuttle), aimed with the right stick {rs}.
{select} lists pause, chat and the next event. Hold {select} for the Menus mode (the main menu, the army painter, the lobbies) and hold it again to come back. {start} (F10) is the game menu; {east} cancels.
The keys can't be changed in the game. They're the defaults as listed for the Definitive Edition, which keeps the original's keys, not checked on this version: the commands on {r3} and next builder and idle military are the likeliest to differ. Guide + {west} opens the on-screen keyboard for chat.
On the campaign map, {rt} picks a territory to attack and {start} opens the menu.'''

